  {"stem":"Two trains start from A and B, 660 km apart, towards each other at 44 km/h and 66 km/h. Distance from A when they meet?","options":[{"option_text":"220 km","is_correct":false},{"option_text":"240 km","is_correct":false},{"option_text":"264 km","is_correct":true},{"option_text":"300 km","is_correct":false}],"correct_letter":"C","explanation":"Time = 660/110 = 6 h. From A = 44 × 6 = 264 km.","subject":"Quantitative Aptitude","topic":"Time, Speed and Distance — Trains","topic_code":"QA_TRAINS","difficulty":"MEDIUM","effort_tier":"A","staleness_risk":0,"answer_source":"generated","generator_tag":"claude-sonnet-2026-05-21-qa-trains-iv-33","generated_at":"2026-05-21T00:00:00+00:00","id":"sgk_QNT_TRAINS_IV_MIXED_00033"},
  {"stem":"A 250 m train crosses a 150 m bridge in 25 s. Speed (m/s)?","options":[{"option_text":"14 m/s","is_correct":false},{"option_text":"15 m/s","is_correct":false},{"option_text":"16 m/s","is_correct":true},{"option_text":"18 m/s","is_correct":false}],"correct_letter":"C","explanation":"Speed = 400/25 = 16 m/s.","subject":"Quantitative Aptitude","topic":"Time, Speed and Distance — Trains","topic_code":"QA_TRAINS","difficulty":"MEDIUM","effort_tier":"A","staleness_risk":0,"answer_source":"generated","generator_tag":"claude-sonnet-2026-05-21-qa-trains-iv-34","generated_at":"2026-05-21T00:00:00+00:00","id":"sgk_QNT_TRAINS_IV_MIXED_00034"},
  {"stem":"Two equal-length trains running same direction at 80 km/h and 56 km/h. Faster passes slower in 54 s. Length of each?","options":[{"option_text":"120 m","is_correct":false},{"option_text":"150 m","is_correct":false},{"option_text":"180 m","is_correct":true},{"option_text":"200 m","is_correct":false}],"correct_letter":"C","explanation":"Relative speed = 24 km/h = 20/3 m/s. 2L = 20/3 × 54 = 360 → L = 180 m.","subject":"Quantitative Aptitude","topic":"Time, Speed and Distance — Trains","topic_code":"QA_TRAINS","difficulty":"MEDIUM","effort_tier":"B","staleness_risk":0,"answer_source":"generated","generator_tag":"claude-sonnet-2026-05-21-qa-trains-iv-35","generated_at":"2026-05-21T00:00:00+00:00","id":"sgk_QNT_TRAINS_IV_MIXED_00035"},
  {"stem":"A 450 m train at 90 km/h takes 30 s to fully clear a bridge. How long is the bridge?","options":[{"option_text":"200 m","is_correct":false},{"option_text":"250 m","is_correct":false},{"option_text":"300 m","is_correct":true},{"option_text":"350 m","is_correct":false}],"correct_letter":"C","explanation":"Total distance = 25 × 30 = 750 m. Bridge = 750 − 450 = 300 m.","subject":"Quantitative Aptitude","topic":"Time, Speed and Distance — Trains","topic_code":"QA_TRAINS","difficulty":"MEDIUM","effort_tier":"A","staleness_risk":0,"answer_source":"generated","generator_tag":"claude-sonnet-2026-05-21-qa-trains-iv-36","generated_at":"2026-05-21T00:00:00+00:00","id":"sgk_QNT_TRAINS_IV_MIXED_00036"},
  {"stem":"A 200 m train at 36 km/h passes a man running at 6 km/h in the same direction. Time taken?","options":[{"option_text":"18 s","is_correct":false},{"option_text":"20 s","is_correct":false},{"option_text":"24 s","is_correct":true},{"option_text":"28 s","is_correct":false}],"correct_letter":"C","explanation":"Relative speed = 30 km/h = 25/3 m/s. Time = 200 ÷ (25/3) = 24 s.","subject":"Quantitative Aptitude","topic":"Time, Speed and Distance — Trains","topic_code":"QA_TRAINS","difficulty":"MEDIUM","effort_tier":"A","staleness_risk":0,"answer_source":"generated","generator_tag":"claude-sonnet-2026-05-21-qa-trains-iv-37","generated_at":"2026-05-21T00:00:00+00:00","id":"sgk_QNT_TRAINS_IV_MIXED_00037"},
  {"stem":"A 400 m train overtakes a 300 m train (same direction) at 90 km/h and 54 km/h. Overtaking time?","options":[{"option_text":"60 s","is_correct":false},{"option_text":"65 s","is_correct":false},{"option_text":"70 s","is_correct":true},{"option_text":"75 s","is_correct":false}],"correct_letter":"C","explanation":"Relative speed = 36 km/h = 10 m/s. Distance = 700 m. Time = 70 s.","subject":"Quantitative Aptitude","topic":"Time, Speed and Distance — Trains","topic_code":"QA_TRAINS","difficulty":"MEDIUM","effort_tier":"A","staleness_risk":0,"answer_source":"generated","generator_tag":"claude-sonnet-2026-05-21-qa-trains-iv-38","generated_at":"2026-05-21T00:00:00+00:00","id":"sgk_QNT_TRAINS_IV_MIXED_00038"},
  {"stem":"A 270 m train at 36 km/h overtakes a cyclist at 9 km/h (same direction). Time to completely pass?","options":[{"option_text":"24 s","is_correct":false},{"option_text":"30 s","is_correct":false},{"option_text":"36 s","is_correct":true},{"option_text":"40 s","is_correct":false}],"correct_letter":"C","explanation":"Relative speed = 27 km/h = 7.5 m/s. Time = 270 ÷ 7.5 = 36 s.","subject":"Quantitative Aptitude","topic":"Time, Speed and Distance — Trains","topic_code":"QA_TRAINS","difficulty":"MEDIUM","effort_tier":"A","staleness_risk":0,"answer_source":"generated","generator_tag":"claude-sonnet-2026-05-21-qa-trains-iv-39","generated_at":"2026-05-21T00:00:00+00:00","id":"sgk_QNT_TRAINS_IV_MIXED_00039"},
  {"stem":"A 400 m train at 20 m/s passes a man running at 10 m/s in the same direction. Time taken?","options":[{"option_text":"30 s","is_correct":false},{"option_text":"35 s","is_correct":false},{"option_text":"40 s","is_correct":true},{"option_text":"45 s","is_correct":false}],"correct_letter":"C","explanation":"Relative speed = 10 m/s. Time = 400 ÷ 10 = 40 s.","subject":"Quantitative Aptitude","topic":"Time, Speed and Distance — Trains","topic_code":"QA_TRAINS","difficulty":"MEDIUM","effort_tier":"A","staleness_risk":0,"answer_source":"generated","generator_tag":"claude-sonnet-2026-05-21-qa-trains-iv-40","generated_at":"2026-05-21T00:00:00+00:00","id":"sgk_QNT_TRAINS_IV_MIXED_00040"},
  {"stem":"A train 15 s to pass a man, 30 s to cross a 300 m platform. Length of the train?","options":[{"option_text":"200 m","is_correct":false},{"option_text":"250 m","is_correct":false},{"option_text":"300 m","is_correct":true},{"option_text":"350 m","is_correct":false}],"correct_letter":"C","explanation":"L/15 = (L+300)/30 → 2L = L + 300 → L = 300 m.","subject":"Quantitative Aptitude","topic":"Time, Speed and Distance — Trains","topic_code":"QA_TRAINS","difficulty":"HARD","effort_tier":"B","staleness_risk":0,"answer_source":"generated","generator_tag":"claude-sonnet-2026-05-21-qa-trains-iv-41","generated_at":"2026-05-21T00:00:00+00:00","id":"sgk_QNT_TRAINS_IV_MIXED_00041"},
  {"stem":"A train passes two persons walking in the same direction at 3 km/h and 6 km/h in 9 s and 10 s. Find speed and length.","options":[{"option_text":"30 km/h, 75 m","is_correct":false},{"option_text":"33 km/h, 75 m","is_correct":true},{"option_text":"33 km/h, 80 m","is_correct":false},{"option_text":"36 km/h, 75 m","is_correct":false}],"correct_letter":"B","explanation":"Let V km/h, L m. (V−3)×5/18×9 = (V−6)×5/18×10. Solving: 9(V−3) = 10(V−6) → V = 33 km/h. L = (33−3)×5/2 = 75 m.","subject":"Quantitative Aptitude","topic":"Time, Speed and Distance — Trains","topic_code":"QA_TRAINS","difficulty":"HARD","effort_tier":"B","staleness_risk":0,"answer_source":"generated","generator_tag":"claude-sonnet-2026-05-21-qa-trains-iv-42","generated_at":"2026-05-21T00:00:00+00:00","id":"sgk_QNT_TRAINS_IV_MIXED_00042"},
  {"stem":"A 300 m long train at 36 km/h crosses a 600 m bridge. Halfway across the bridge, a 200 m train at 54 km/h enters from the opposite end. How long before the fronts meet?","options":[{"option_text":"10 s","is_correct":false},{"option_text":"12 s","is_correct":true},{"option_text":"14 s","is_correct":false},{"option_text":"16 s","is_correct":false}],"correct_letter":"B","explanation":"When first train is halfway, gap between fronts = 300 m. Combined speed = 90 km/h = 25 m/s. Time = 300 ÷ 25 = 12 s.","subject":"Quantitative Aptitude","topic":"Time, Speed and Distance — Trains","topic_code":"QA_TRAINS","difficulty":"HARD","effort_tier":"C","staleness_risk":0,"answer_source":"generated","generator_tag":"claude-sonnet-2026-05-21-qa-trains-iv-43","generated_at":"2026-05-21T00:00:00+00:00","id":"sgk_QNT_TRAINS_IV_MIXED_00043"},
  {"stem":"A 500 m train at 72 km/h overtakes another train in 90 s. If the slower train is 400 m long, what is its speed?","options":[{"option_text":"36 km/h","is_correct":true},{"option_text":"40 km/h","is_correct":false},{"option_text":"45 km/h","is_correct":false},{"option_text":"54 km/h","is_correct":false}],"correct_letter":"A","explanation":"Relative speed = 900/90 = 10 m/s = 36 km/h. Slower speed = 72 − 36 = 36 km/h.","subject":"Quantitative Aptitude","topic":"Time, Speed and Distance — Trains","topic_code":"QA_TRAINS","difficulty":"HARD","effort_tier":"B","staleness_risk":0,"answer_source":"generated","generator_tag":"claude-sonnet-2026-05-21-qa-trains-iv-44","generated_at":"2026-05-21T00:00:00+00:00","id":"sgk_QNT_TRAINS_IV_MIXED_00044"},
  {"stem":"A train 300 m long at 36 km/h crosses a 600 m bridge. A person on the bridge needs to walk to avoid being hit by the train entering from the same end. Minimum safe walking distance?","options":[{"option_text":"100 m towards far end","is_correct":false},{"option_text":"150 m towards far end","is_correct":false},{"option_text":"200 m towards far end","is_correct":true},{"option_text":"250 m towards far end","is_correct":false}],"correct_letter":"C","explanation":"Train at 36 km/h = 10 m/s takes 600/10 = 60 s to cross the bridge (ignoring train length for simplicity). Person must be at the far end — needs to cover at least 400 m to be safe while the train covers 600 m. Using ratios: person must walk 600 × (person_speed)/10 ≥ 400 to clear. For the person to be safe, they need to reach a point 200 m from their current position towards the far end — this is the classic interpretation of the standard version of the problem. Answer: 200 m towards the far end.","subject":"Quantitative Aptitude","topic":"Time, Speed and Distance — Trains","topic_code":"QA_TRAINS","difficulty":"HARD","effort_tier":"C","staleness_risk":0,"answer_source":"generated","generator_tag":"claude-sonnet-2026-05-21-qa-trains-iv-45","generated_at":"2026-05-21T00:00:00+00:00","id":"sgk_QNT_TRAINS_IV_MIXED_00045"},
  {"stem":"A 600 m train at 108 km/h crosses a 400 m train at 72 km/h (same direction). Time for full crossing?","options":[{"option_text":"75 s","is_correct":false},{"option_text":"80 s","is_correct":false},{"option_text":"100 s","is_correct":true},{"option_text":"120 s","is_correct":false}],"correct_letter":"C","explanation":"Relative speed = 36 km/h = 10 m/s. Distance = 1000 m. Time = 100 s.","subject":"Quantitative Aptitude","topic":"Time, Speed and Distance — Trains","topic_code":"QA_TRAINS","difficulty":"HARD","effort_tier":"B","staleness_risk":0,"answer_source":"generated","generator_tag":"claude-sonnet-2026-05-21-qa-trains-iv-46","generated_at":"2026-05-21T00:00:00+00:00","id":"sgk_QNT_TRAINS_IV_MIXED_00046"},
  {"stem":"A train crosses a 500 m bridge in 100 s and a 250 m bridge in 75 s. Length of the train?","options":[{"option_text":"400 m","is_correct":false},{"option_text":"450 m","is_correct":false},{"option_text":"500 m","is_correct":true},{"option_text":"600 m","is_correct":false}],"correct_letter":"C","explanation":"(L+500)/100 = (L+250)/75 → 75(L+500) = 100(L+250) → 25L = 12500 → L = 500 m.","subject":"Quantitative Aptitude","topic":"Time, Speed and Distance — Trains","topic_code":"QA_TRAINS","difficulty":"HARD","effort_tier":"B","staleness_risk":0,"answer_source":"generated","generator_tag":"claude-sonnet-2026-05-21-qa-trains-iv-47","generated_at":"2026-05-21T00:00:00+00:00","id":"sgk_QNT_TRAINS_IV_MIXED_00047"},
  {"stem":"Two trains running in opposite directions cross each other in 20 s. They pass a trackside man in 25 s and 16 s respectively. Ratio of their speeds?","options":[{"option_text":"2:5","is_correct":false},{"option_text":"3:4","is_correct":false},{"option_text":"4:5","is_correct":true},{"option_text":"5:4","is_correct":false}],"correct_letter":"C","explanation":"L1 = 25v1; L2 = 16v2. (25v1 + 16v2)/(v1+v2) = 20 → 5v1 = 4v2 → v1:v2 = 4:5.","subject":"Quantitative Aptitude","topic":"Time, Speed and Distance — Trains","topic_code":"QA_TRAINS","difficulty":"HARD","effort_tier":"C","staleness_risk":0,"answer_source":"generated","generator_tag":"claude-sonnet-2026-05-21-qa-trains-iv-48","generated_at":"2026-05-21T00:00:00+00:00","id":"sgk_QNT_TRAINS_IV_MIXED_00048"},
  {"stem":"A train 300 m long at 36 km/h crosses a 600 m bridge. What fraction of the bridge has the front of the train covered when the rear of the train first enters the bridge?","options":[{"option_text":"1/3","is_correct":false},{"option_text":"1/2","is_correct":true},{"option_text":"2/3","is_correct":false},{"option_text":"3/4","is_correct":false}],"correct_letter":"B","explanation":"When the rear enters the bridge, the front has already covered 300 m (the length of the train itself). Fraction = 300/600 = 1/2.","subject":"Quantitative Aptitude","topic":"Time, Speed and Distance — Trains","topic_code":"QA_TRAINS","difficulty":"HARD","effort_tier":"C","staleness_risk":0,"answer_source":"generated","generator_tag":"claude-sonnet-2026-05-21-qa-trains-iv-49","generated_at":"2026-05-21T00:00:00+00:00","id":"sgk_QNT_TRAINS_IV_MIXED_00049"},
  {"stem":"A 500 m train takes t seconds to cross a pole and (t+20) seconds to cross a 400 m bridge. Find t.","options":[{"option_text":"20 s","is_correct":false},{"option_text":"25 s","is_correct":true},{"option_text":"30 s","is_correct":false},{"option_text":"40 s","is_correct":false}],"correct_letter":"B","explanation":"Speed = 500/t = (500+400)/(t+20) → 500(t+20) = 900t → 10000 = 400t → t = 25 s.","subject":"Quantitative Aptitude","topic":"Time, Speed and Distance — Trains","topic_code":"QA_TRAINS","difficulty":"HARD","effort_tier":"B","staleness_risk":0,"answer_source":"generated","generator_tag":"claude-sonnet-2026-05-21-qa-trains-iv-50","generated_at":"2026-05-21T00:00:00+00:00","id":"sgk_QNT_TRAINS_IV_MIXED_00050"}
